{"title":"2026 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(easier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (easier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Easier_AM-GM)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Easier AM-GM)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(0_tech)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (0 tech)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(easiest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (easiest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(SFFT)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (SFFT)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be distinct positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/0245ea6143a8becce8cad0af8f49b63670b5746f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+c=c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b6c57a9202479f622af12cf8ae8b9f6ea66da52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2\\ge 4c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af962256f9f59fbd080b334112c2fb44bc10351d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=c^2-c=c(c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"21\" />. WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5bac75f1fb89cfc176d82d5aa8db36bd61bc89d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;\\sqrt{c(c-1)}&gt;c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"178\" height=\"35\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, this implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a60ef349a28cf08abc968556e14b07c7c46c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/607b0e2df9b93576cc8b7f8e25b9e78a7ab66b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />, so let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/8438db636244ef1431e710fc0ccac8f42cd0c33a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = c+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b614bb5f52bb423442c81a9012b2c44e5ab753f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+k \\mid c(c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c79c5d7cf3fb61f15b89944a30ee811bcd6c4774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+k = c_1 c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca74b619d2290cea48b643854641bb9c2944d7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1 \\mid c - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc0cc911213105660e2b749586cb5b8cacdcc1e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2\\mid c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a11433bbda41b708391dcebe3224370e013457.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_1 \\leq \\text{gcd }(c-1, c+k)\\leq k+1\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e83e335424f3cc66009c67281e6e074c8013f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_2 \\leq \\text{gcd }(c, c+k)\\leq k\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/920f12cc22a6fd0bd48d564224532175c306ad7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+k\\leq k(k+1)\\implies k\\geq \\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"22\" />. Finishing up, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2cbd4c4ddabbcf1fcf047d2e3ad9369d21a7b82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=c+k\\geq c+\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61d2f8168d3db899c6beff6eb094f983a781b82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{c^2-c}{a}\\leq c-\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"41\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b458f1be5bd9a3e85d5f04422ed6abd38da49c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a-b\\geq 2\\sqrt{c}\\implies (a-b)^2\\geq 4c\\]\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" /> and the proof is complete. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~sillybone\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewrite the condition as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bc437bfbe7acac344900ea39e65ea7a20cdeb1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=c^2-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />. Then examine the LHS:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68ac464cdae360d7e5c7b8fde0b1939e09b778a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2=(a+b)^2-4ab=(a+b)^2+4c-4c^2\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d1a9545d566fd5bdc8cfc939559cd18326a280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=c(c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are distinct meaning one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and the other is smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b404b7e6fc336380702c33035a5d6a7b34e7b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=c+n,b=c+m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43e0559cb0239b98c18732db5e1ab2c3b3f4d41e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nm&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />. So\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0ba63de3c88571efadadcdcd7fa0c0f39c23331d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ab=c^2+(n+m)c+nm=c^2-c\\implies c=\\frac{-nm}{n+m+1}\\]\" width=\"432\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1bb51afff5fb240f36891f4551733ba8a674630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/40013a8df870677b64e95d1d092c9fdd880a6fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-nm&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114524e07b3eb63cedf4dc3e3e1792a1470c5756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+m+1&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/801b47ae438758187fc0bc81ba245d2dc49e81a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" /> are both integers which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83ddf6ae91f83dff6a6fb029addb21dfe1563913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+m\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982e6ad32bdf4b3d6e6275ae8f02f460687c60e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\ge 2c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />.\nPlugging this in to the inequality gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/039e5f2a69e5adb46a0ba33a6d6c2ce2a072c11a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2=(a+b)^2-4ab=(a+b)^2+4c-4c^2\\ge (2c)^2+4c-4c^2=4c\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>~WYC10041\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28easier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(easier)\">Solution 3 (easier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (easier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By AM-GM,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/6/686d88e3741333340e1faa91a99825316cc8701f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+b\\ge 2\\sqrt{c^2-c}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"19\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce7bfd334c5cb1fd201b90a763ce6b9184de331d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\le 2c-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6a78f4c463716c5cdfdd20cd118bbc937cd417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c-2\\ge 2\\sqrt{c^2-c}\\implies 4c^2-8c+4\\ge 4c^2-4c\\implies c\\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"467\" height=\"21\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e4cc644ec8a1c3623c13ed3d14904096a0d87b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c1b471285ba9eddebe00c19acc0084576a884b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=c^2-c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, contradiction.\n</p><p>Next, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe21d216f4f5f4f06f5ed0723610607d86dc17f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=2c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> are the roots of the quadratic\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f76e89a282df892e112935caa532cad4e14920.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t^2-(2c-1)t+(c^2-c)=0\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"20\" />\nwhich has roots at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb3ea2e955d39fdbd0615c0f99e1094887d5bb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=c,c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. But then one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, contradicting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> distinct, so we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982e6ad32bdf4b3d6e6275ae8f02f460687c60e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\ge 2c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />. Then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/4/f748f71b97b192f63dbede73e14d1e120b35785d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+b\\ge 2c\\implies (a+b)^2\\ge 4c^2\\implies (a-b)^2\\ge 4c^2-4ab=4c\\]\" width=\"489\" height=\"20\" />\nas desired.\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Easier_AM-GM.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Easier_AM-GM)\">Solution 4 (Easier AM-GM)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Easier AM-GM)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0e98d9393c406a69e25bef89a98f75b6ec9a135.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Lemma}$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>For all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95c70ec01b46b58ca7a4a7001a6bab390a198815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, the following inequality suffices.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c242d17046a115d0748797335e3ddda6f13f997.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a-b}{2} \\ge \\sqrt{ab}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80a97bf0fc3bbeaf1fae16b7d9c9e29030b9a01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Proof of the Lemma}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"171\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa30e2beb1820f6b39f6251023709c8165cefc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> in the AM-GM inequality.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a9d0341989b0aeae5257b85c47b26a5c91b37ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a-b}{2} \\ge \\sqrt{-ab} ~~~~~~~~~~ \\text{(1.1)}\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Then the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/0410593a1fb5a796bae6525853c19b35a08eb4e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{-ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"21\" /> holds only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95c70ec01b46b58ca7a4a7001a6bab390a198815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. Then the result becomes \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/43659de05ee44c7ce401c037b946e79e4f5b60d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a-b}{2} \\ge \\sqrt{ab} ~~~~~~~~~~ \\text{(1.2)}\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>hence proven.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4ec0fd14305ebf36f69188782909cdee8b72827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{USAJMO Q1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>AM-GM and rearrangement of the inequality states that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2500e79ce6da7bb139a4cc3c328aa1f64fd387.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ab \\le \\frac{(a+b)^2}{4}\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>and thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982144630b54dfc592a7a5b1b67e814671858eca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4ab \\le (a+b)^2\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The application of 1.1 gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93be305952e8c6402a352db8f52ceb7bff4a5694.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2 \\ge -4ab\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/4842444e5daae6563aef39a034fc3041d8579f0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-(a-b)^2 \\le 4ab\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>And thus the inequality\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15b8b3137e47914d0ba0e16c73a5b75300ce841d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-(a-b)^2 \\le 4ab \\le (a+b)^2 ~~~~~~~~~~ \\text{(1.3)}\\]\" width=\"298\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Rearranging 1.3 gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e7838b359cfa6bd76e3a53d5e550e6f7f30122aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-(a^2 + b^2) \\le 2ab \\le a^2 + b^2\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14b229cadea3a10acf93c8066dd09678ec9f2b9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-(a-b)^2 \\le 0 \\le (a-b)^2\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>It then follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2513ae423b392278e2613b4152185709523cb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2 \\ge 0 ~~~~~~~~~~ \\text{(1.4)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Applying the lemma, particularly result 1.2 and rearranging gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d75cf8fa58c1ec73ab38ffbf5e58a515130a4f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2 \\ge 4ab\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Note that then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c747c0c29194fca16abe76299521a8e862eb944.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4ab \\le 0\\]\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> as a direct result from 1.1. It is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/86591f989298bebbb059058a523555235d48a08e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = c(c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e17c75c8b4991fd2ea54a84ef6542d7a168e60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c(c-1) \\le 0\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> in which equality holds if one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f2924e05b65d0a1887d309cb3aad442e9ccee0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> is 0, in which the result is trivial. Otherwise if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/9337e54baae79dd60fd40e79fce64fe6b98a51a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-1 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, division of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f2924e05b65d0a1887d309cb3aad442e9ccee0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> into 0 gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/34078728eb11fa562c017612ca4b2314d2e59688.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. This result then shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48b8bf81963cc7068474eb3ea19566f93b93e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4c \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e1b95cfef69eb996b66eee12846c4cc3c46ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48b8bf81963cc7068474eb3ea19566f93b93e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4c \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, it is proven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d03fa66a979e1076b04eca1a497276b36e61afe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2 \\ge 4c \\quad \\square\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p>Question to author: How is 4c≤0 if it is given that a,b,c are distinct positive integers?\n</p><p>Because we are under the condition of the Lemma, remember! We take an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/9/6e910fbdee9e49ecd361de716bd6c929f73979aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\mapsto -b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />. The only reason the final inequality stands is because at the end, even after obtaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf28da8b74a8b3196663273bde6347b29de81e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4c \\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> we can still formulate a map <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/13245530e8cf4cd057bd8dd0de5e76370abf4757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-c \\mapsto c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> such that we shift <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a644e784380bf70cd389a206ae0475c1458dfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> by some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> so the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19ac102282ae64db520954c4ef0d66b34de5e86b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4c +x \\leq x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> holds. Similarly, we can shift the RHS <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/392b9c02b3d65637e015a0aa33df3164f79df79c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" /> by the same <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. This unique <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the equilibrium factor in respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a644e784380bf70cd389a206ae0475c1458dfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, which is why the Lemma still proves the claim correct.\n</p><p>It is hard to see at first, maybe I should have clarified... if required, I will rewrite the solution. But as I've heard from others it is fine as is, so if I get another question then I'll try to rewrite it. Too lazy rn though!&#160;:(. Nice question, I'll try to be more specific later on...\n</p><p>Same person who wrote the question: Ty, this really helped!\n</p><p><b>Remark</b>\n</p><p>Another way one could have seen this inequality hold is the fact <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a65fe5f396d8c182d88144d00e26156435e0743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> expands quadratically whereas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a644e784380bf70cd389a206ae0475c1458dfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> expands linearly. Both are centred correspondingly to the centre/origin  hence the inequality must hold true. Indeed, a graphical approach can be used along with the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/86591f989298bebbb059058a523555235d48a08e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = c(c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.280_tech.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(0_tech)\">Solution 5 (0 tech)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (0 tech)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb4fba5d5c61615c187597189ab82d278b50131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4c = 4c^2-4ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, it suffices to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a9a47af0823506856ab4f5447c955a24067166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\ge 2c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Note that by common sense, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/86591f989298bebbb059058a523555235d48a08e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = c(c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44608e00263ecf9d87b62ddeda0d1eaf1edbfb4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b \\ge 2c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />. However, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/868bb4c924c36887e50d478e6c44c08db1c2f7fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ne b \\ne c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26fb7db9e06189a002df232ab12116df98432ae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\ne 2c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a9a47af0823506856ab4f5447c955a24067166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\ge 2c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Equality occurs a lot; for example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea3ecd838fce91e79ea1ea045fc3fe0fa593328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c) = (2, 6, 4) \\quad \\mathbb{Q.E.D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28easiest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(easiest)\">Solution 6 (easiest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (easiest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87b5d0a6c104e3cee03a3554b67a92c50d56751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+c=c^2 \\implies ab=c(c-1) \\implies a+b \\geq 2c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"403\" height=\"21\" /> where equality is achieved by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281572e13c58f7082937a96d2d439377740fa108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a,b\\}=\\{c-1,c\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" />, but this violates distinctness, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a9a47af0823506856ab4f5447c955a24067166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\ge 2c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />. We can finish with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc352e7d2158526641ef138ce45661a9474e60f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2 = (a+b)^2 - 4ab \\ge (2c)^2 - 4c(c-1) = 4c\\]\" width=\"390\" height=\"20\" />\nas desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Baihly2024\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28SFFT.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(SFFT)\">Video Solution (SFFT)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (SFFT)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/den_txoy5Qs?si=KEuC3a7V2M-D4OXW\">https://youtu.be/den_txoy5Qs?si=KEuC3a7V2M-D4OXW</a> - Continuum Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO\" title=\"2026 USAJMO\">2026 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017222512\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.108 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 6